        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "091447d3-40f3-598f-b959-2093321b7ce6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Helen Fraser, Roman Polanski, Catherine Deneuve, Ian Hendry, John Fraser, Yvonne Furneaux, Kika Mirylees, Victoria Alcock\n- Works: Billy Liar, Repulsion, Sylvia Hollamby\n- Topics: acting careers, film roles, television roles\n\nFacts:\n- Helen Fraser was born Helen Margaret Stronach on 15 June 1942 in Oldham, Lancashire.\n- Helen Fraser is an English actress who has appeared in many television series since the early 1960s.\n- Helen Fraser is known internationally for her roles in Billy Liar (1963) and Repulsion (1965).\n- Repulsion is a 1965 British psychological horror film directed by Roman Polanski.\n- Repulsion stars Catherine Deneuve, Ian Hendry, John Fraser, and Yvonne Furneaux.\n- Helen Fraser portrayed Sylvia Hollamby from the first episode in 1999 until the last in 2006.\n- Sylvia Hollamby was the longest-serving prison officer on the show.\n- Julie Johnston, played by Kika Mirylees, and Julie Saunders, played by Victoria Alcock, were the only other characters to last all eight series.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
